WEBVTT

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.400
Hi there. Welcome.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.150
Do you want a Wonder Egg?

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:19.310
It's hard.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.520
What? You're not sure yet?

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.310
Don't hesitate.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.600
Have courage and believe in yourself.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.900
Crack the Egg.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.060
Shut up!

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.600
It has the thing you want in it.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.440
It has your wish in it.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.020
If you crack it in the Egg world...

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.020
...and if you clear your mission...

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.440
She's a little warm.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.520
You might be able to get it back.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.020
Your friend.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.650
Your memories.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.520
Your loved one.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.190
The first time's free.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:04.810
After that, bring your wallet.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:08.520
What? How do we make the Eggs?

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.520
That's a trade secret.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:14.400
We can't just tell you.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.900
I know: Let us tell you about
our regular customers instead.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.020
A group of four charming young girls.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:26.020
It's our story that no one else
knows about, right?

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:32.150
A story... that no one knows about.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:36.020
Listen, and then make up your mind

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:39.850
about whether you'll bring home an Egg.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.990
Wonder Egg Priority

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.990
Episode 8: 'The Happy Friendship Plan'

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:43.480
I'm going out.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.270
Huh?

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.230
This is...

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:01.310
This isn't reality. It's a dream.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:05.400
Or, well, let's call it the "Egg world."

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.810
A world only people who've
broken an Egg can connect to.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.190
It's strongly influenced
by your mental landscape.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:17.560
And under certain conditions,
you can share that world with other people.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:18.650
Fun, right?

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:20.230
You synchronized.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.770
We what?

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:27.310
You fell asleep near each other,
and at almost the same time, so...

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.520
But why aren't we in my dream?

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.190
You're pulled by whoever's
feelings are stronger.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:38.060
Break the Egg.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.400
The what?

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.730
The Wonder Egg.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:46.480
When you crack a Wonder Egg,
a girl emerges from inside it.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:54.150
They're girls who approached death
of their own will and left this life,

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.600
but you will protect them.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.150
What from?

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:01.650
From Seeno Evils and Wonder Killers.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:08.060
What are they?!

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.440
You ought to know!

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.850
They're Seeno Evils!

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.100
What's that?!

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.560
No idea!

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.400
Now, let's get right to one of our regulars.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.980
Her name is Ai Ohto.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:25.810
A 14-year-old with mismatched eye colors.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.310
A middle-school second year.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.600
Ai! Your teacher is here.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.020
There's no need to force her to get up, ma'am.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:34.150
Ai's

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.900
When she met us, she wouldn't go to school.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.900
She says she was bullied for her heterochromia.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:45.350
Well, that's not why she was
skipping school, though.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.100
What's that?

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.650
A game.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.730
Do you like games?

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:56.230
Ai's meeting with Koito Nagase,
a new student in her class,

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:58.900
changed her destiny in a big way.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.810
It's mysterious.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.020
You shouldn't hide it.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:05.350
I get bullied for it.

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:06.690
Always.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.850
It's pretty.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.850
Be my friend.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:27.350
Let's be best friends.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.810
If we could, I'd be happy.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.770
Me, too.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.980
She finally made a best friend.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.100
But one day, she lost her without warning.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.850
Oh, no. What happened?

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.350
Classic harassment.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.810
Why would they do this to you?

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:54.600
Because you're my friend?

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.770
That's not it.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.730
They say Mr. Sawaki is
giving me special treatment.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.100
I think they're jealous.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.520
I'm sorry. I was scared.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:09.900
Scared of being left out.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:15.150
Are you okay?

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:23.810
Did you get the video?

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.020
You were scared, huh?

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.020
Sorry.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.310
I'm so sorry.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.600
It's fine.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.150
I know you tried your best.

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.560
I'm sorry.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.230
It's my fault.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:42.560
Because I betrayed you.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.020
Koito Nagase committed suicide.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:46.480
Why'd she die?

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.600
What was Ai lacking?

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.560
Who pushed Koito toward it?

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:55.350
Ai is fighting to get back
the best friend she lost.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:58.400
I'm done pretending not to see!

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.480
I understand.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:05.600
There was a part of me that resented her.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.020
We were friends, so why didn't she talk to me?

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:11.100
Why?!

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.020
If she'd asked me to die with her,

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.310
I'd...

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:23.310
I'd have...!

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:27.270
Now I'm mad!

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:35.650
A mission's victory condition
is to defeat a Wonder Killer,

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:39.440
a symbol of the Egg girl's discord,
obsession, or trauma.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:44.650
In the Egg world, you're immortal.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.810
And your physical abilities
dramatically increase.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:51.100
Now I'm really mad!

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:57.190
You may be immortal, but watch out for injuries.

00:06:57.190 --> 00:07:00.270
If you come back hurt, you'll end up like her.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.600
Neiru Aonuma.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.150
Here's my contact info.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.730
Message me when you want to change plans.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:10.940
I'll buy Eggs on odd days;
you buy them on even days.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:08.900
Huh?!

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.100
We won't have to meet again.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:18.230
Neiru's a girl genius. She's just 14,
but she runs her own company.

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.060
It's huge.

00:07:19.060 --> 00:07:22.310
She's calm, not very talkative,

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:26.270
and not very outgoing.

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:27.270
Here.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:30.100
Thanks.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.560
This smells amazing!

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:37.980
You're right.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.100
Right?

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:49.900
You're trusting, Ai. You forgive easily.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.810
I'm hopeless that way.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:56.020
You're lovely that way.

00:07:57.480 --> 00:08:00.310
You're hopeless and lovely that way.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:04.980
We need someone like that sometimes,
or we'll never be saved.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.850
She seems to have taken to Ai,

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.850
A capable woman actually spoils them.

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:12.230
but she's a little too harsh on Rika.

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:09.440
Why are you looking at me?

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:12.230
Because it's your turn.

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:15.190
You're an anachronistic fool.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:16.600
Who are you calling "fool"?

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.020
Stop, fool.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.400
Coochy-coochy-coo...

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.650
How about here?

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:26.150
Still, she has her charms.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.150
They really get along, huh?

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:26.900
Yeah.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:27.560
One of those " <i>tsunderes</i> "?

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:28.940
No, we--

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:31.230
What about this spot?

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:39.560
Neiru is buying Eggs and fighting
to get back her little sister.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.440
Who are you fighting for?

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:44.230
You're sure it's not for yourself?

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:47.310
You don't like who you are now, so you go.

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:49.150
Even if you're scared.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:51.440
You want to change the self you hate.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:54.100
Sorry, but I have to go.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.650
What for?!

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:59.730
For someone selfish enough to...
kill themselves...?

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:02.560
Rika, Neiru's trying to save her sister.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.350
Wrong.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.350
My sister stabbed me.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.810
Huh?

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:10.770
Then, she ran away and jumped off a bridge.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:12.480
That's...

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.900
That's what they told me
when I woke up in the ICU.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:18.850
Then you've got even less of a reason.

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:22.060
The scar aches and keeps me awake.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:27.020
But the pain has faded
since I started going there.

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:31.350
When I try to forget her,
my scar aches, like a curse.

00:09:31.350 --> 00:09:33.560
That's why I go.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.600
No other reason.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:39.230
It's for me.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:41.650
Girls become adults.

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:45.350
The miraculous beauty of a butterfly emerging.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.190
A brief moment.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:52.980
You're pretty, too. Why don't you die?

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.600
Why not die when you're at your most beautiful?

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.810
Why cling to a meaningless life?

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:57.810
This isn't good.

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:01.900
Hey, why don't you die?

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:09.270
Mirror, mirror on the wall,
who's the fairest of them all?

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:03.690
Why don't you?

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:09.270
Tell me!

00:10:09.270 --> 00:10:12.100
I'm going to blow your mind.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:17.230
"Why don't I die," huh?

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:21.020
You tempted me to die, didn't you?

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.730
Experience gained in the Egg world

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:29.690
is directly reflected in reality.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:34.770
For example, as you run and jump there,
your athleticism improves.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:40.940
It seems like fighting there puts
a heavy strain on our bodies.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:43.230
Like high-altitude training?

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:44.230
Yes.

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:48.600
Now you mention it, I think I've
gotten some definition on my abs.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.810
Your wounds heal faster, too,
so heal up before you come back.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.880
When you get back next time

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.880
let's be friends

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:00.310
It might be a bit tough at first.

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:02.770
It takes practice.

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:04.230
I'm going

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:06.060
to change.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:09.350
Don't worry. You can do it, too.

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:12.480
I'm going

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:15.020
to blow your mind.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.690
Stop!

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.690
It's my fault!

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:20.480
Leave me alone!

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:21.320
So...

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.900
You just want attention!

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:29.650
What you really mean is that you want
someone to find you and love you!

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:32.270
So, I won't leave you alone!

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:34.150
I <i>can't</i> leave you alone!

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:37.650
Sorry,

00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:42.100
but that's just abuse!

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:46.310
Now I'm really mad!

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:49.060
Goodbye, coach!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.560
Thank you, Ai.

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:10.400
These aren't Seeno Evils!

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:11.400
They're Haters.

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:15.190
You've done too much to stand out in this world.

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:20.230
Envy and spite created Haters of
you girls from among the Seeno Evils.

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:25.520
They don't have the guts to show
their faces, but they do have madness.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.270
They're strong in groups.

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:29.350
Maybe as strong as a boss.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.270
Run or hide.

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:34.730
They're after you:
the "heroes" in the limelight.

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:37.270
Hide here until the bell rings.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:41.100
You can't clear the mission if you don't fight.

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:44.650
Well, focus on maintaining
the status quo for today.

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.560
I have a solution in mind.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:49.350
But Yae is hurt. It's my fault she--

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.980
Not a problem.

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:54.650
She'll regenerate in as little as
ten minutes in her Egg.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:57.980
Damn, they found us?

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:02.520
Protect the Egg girl until time runs out.
That's your top priority.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:05.150
Society is built on "report, contact, consult."

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.400
Say it out loud and share it.

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:09.940
Our greatest objective is...

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.230
...Wonder...

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.230
...Egg...

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.230
...Priority.

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.980
As we were saying,

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:23.810
this girl is Rika Kawai, a former junior idol.

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:28.690
Remember it as Rika Kawai,
like " <i>kawaii</i> ," since I'm so super cute.

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:33.310
She's talkative, excitable,
and above all, greedy.

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:36.770
Anyway, I forgot my wallet.

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:38.850
Sorry, but could you spot me cash?

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:39.810
Huh?

00:13:39.810 --> 00:13:41.850
Thanks.

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:43.150
Huh?

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.560
Come see Rika again, okay?

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:47.230
Just kidding!

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:51.310
She may seem indomitable at first glance,

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:53.350
but her home life is complicated.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:56.940
My daddy says a beautiful
woman doesn't need a wallet.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:59.850
Someone will always offer to pay for her.

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:02.850
Of course, he got divorced.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:05.150
One of these five is my real daddy.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.310
So, which one is it?

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:11.230
Rika doesn't know her real father.

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:16.310
She obsesses over the father
she's never met and dislikes her mother.

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.150
Well, you see,

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:22.730
I don't know either.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:28.900
I'm pretty sure it's one of these guys, though.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:31.730
You'll meet him someday.

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.690
Someday.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:36.690
I want to meet him now.

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:37.900
Now.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:47.730
No.

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:55.310
The girl Rika wants to save is Chiemi,
a fan from her junior idol days.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:59.480
My little wallet who'd buy me anything.

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:03.020
Chiemi was a real idiot.

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:07.020
She got in line for me dozens,
maybe hundreds of times.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:13.270
She just gave me all her allowance
and New Year's money with a smile.

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:17.520
I believed I had a rich patron.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:21.480
Then one day, I saw her shoplifting in town.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.650
She'd been selling what she took.

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:32.400
Oh, I totally know that feeling.

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:35.650
Yeah, we got sugar daddies for the same reason.

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:37.690
I didn't want that.

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:40.940
So, I told her I'd never be friends with a fan.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:45.270
I said I'd be too embarrassed
to be seen with a fatty in the first place.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:48.310
I said, "Never come back."

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:51.310
After that, another fan told me what happened.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:53.730
Chiemi died.

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:57.440
She was skin and bones, like a mummy.

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:00.690
I couldn't forget her if I wanted to.

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:02.310
This...

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.230
This isn't Chiemi.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:10.100
She regrets that something she said
ended up driving Chiemi to her death.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.440
That's why she fights.

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:14.480
I'll hit you

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:16.400
with a shot to the heart!

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:20.060
Rika?!

00:16:21.270 --> 00:16:24.020
Yeah, but what's with those Haters?

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:28.730
Who asked them to treat us like heroes?
We're not doing this for fun.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:31.690
Didn't you say you "had a solution in mind"?

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:34.900
Yes. Look, here it is now.

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:36.980
Thanks.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:40.980
That case contains things that will support you.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:45.650
Basically, it's what you call a "power up."

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:47.810
So, how do we use them?

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:50.520
First, you hatch them in this world.

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:51.480
Hatch them?

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:53.400
Oh, but don't do it here.

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:56.690
Go home and open them when you're alone.

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:58.100
Why?

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:00.060
They require imprinting.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:03.560
They see whoever meets
their gaze first as their parent.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:06.310
Chant " <i>veni</i> " to call them from their eggs.

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:09.520
" <i>Redi</i> " to return them.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:10.690
<i>Veni</i> .

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:21.810
A snake.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:23.440
Hello?

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:30.810
I'm not sure how to react.

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:31.810
<i>Veni</i> .

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:41.350
He ate it!

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:43.730
Haters are their favorite food.

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:47.310
Envy and spite are their bread and butter.

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:50.480
Okay, I'm counting on you!

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:56.400
And finally, there's Momoe Sawaki.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:59.150
She's a tall, slender girl.

00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:03.650
It was just a day, but I fell in love with you.

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:07.060
I'm really glad that I got to meet you.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:12.480
She says she's often mistaken
for a boy or gets asked out by girls.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:15.020
Don't worry. I'll protect you.

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:19.940
Well, everything she says or does
<i>is</i> cool and handsome.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:26.400
Get lost!

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:30.600
She might be the most "normal" of the four.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:33.770
I love you. I don't want to disappear.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:36.600
I want to stay with you forever.

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:43.350
There are more than you'd think, Haruka.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:46.350
Girls like you, who say they love me.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:51.100
The girl Momoe wants to save is Haruka.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:59.480
She’s got complicated circumstances of her own.

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:03.980
Haruka was willing to see me as a girl.

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:06.520
Touch me.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.560
Your friend who killed herself?

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:09.770
Yeah.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:14.400
But she suddenly took
her clothes off in the infirmary.

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:17.440
She put the moves on you? Whoa.

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:21.520
I got scared and ended up pushing her away.

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:23.690
Excuse us!

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:24.470
Hello.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.810
Oh, my!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:28.600
Aren't you Mr. Sawaki's...?

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.730
Momoe Sawaki. I'm his niece.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:34.520
What a pretty young lady.

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:39.730
And one of Momoe's relatives,
Shuichiro Sawaki, is Ai's teacher.

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:42.270
There's no reason to have a complex.

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:44.980
Your eyes are charming.

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:45.900
Okay.

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:49.270
I'll paint how you look to me.

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:52.850
When it's finished,
I want you to have confidence.

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:56.190
I hear Mr. Sawaki's entering it
in the next exhibition.

00:19:56.190 --> 00:20:00.520
He says he wants to win a prize
and make a living as a painter.

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:02.060
A painting of me?

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:03.940
Confident?

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:06.520
If not, you should decline.

00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:09.900
Mr. Sawaki's future is on the line.

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.150
I...

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:15.270
Shuichiro Sawaki is disturbing Ai's mind.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:18.350
His relationship with Koito Nagase.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.230
His relationship with Ai's mother.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:25.650
Listen calmly, okay?

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:31.520
We've been thinking that
we'd like to start dating.

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:39.230
You mean that my uncle might have
been involved in Koito's suicide?

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:41.270
I told you, there's no way.

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:48.480
I guess we'll never know the truth
unless we bring Koito back and ask her.

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:48.480
Bye-bye, Mr. S.

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:50.770
Goodbye.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:53.900
There might be a factor complicating matters.

00:20:53.900 --> 00:20:55.190
Huh?

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:57.310
Ai likes Mr. Sawaki, too.

00:20:58.560 --> 00:21:03.230
If the truth were easy to find,
no one would struggle.

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.070
Ohto?

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:06.400
The human heart is difficult to fathom.

00:21:04.100 --> 00:21:05.110
What's wrong?

00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:10.850
It looks like Ai's made up her mind
to hunt down the truth,

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:13.940
but we'll have to see where that goes.

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:15.350
I...!

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:23.350
I'm...

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:29.150
...going to go to school!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:40.770
Well, that's pretty much how you use the Eggs.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:43.310
Huh? You don't seem too enthusiastic.

00:21:43.310 --> 00:21:46.400
Hmm. You look as though you can't trust us.

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:50.600
Really? After we broke it all down for you?

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:52.770
That's not nice.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:54.310
We protect these girls.

00:21:54.310 --> 00:21:56.850
From monsters.

00:21:56.850 --> 00:22:00.100
This is a women-only car!

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:02.850
I'm a girl, too!

00:22:02.850 --> 00:22:04.440
Get lost!

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:09.980
I'm worn out.

00:22:09.980 --> 00:22:12.060
I want to be saved.

00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:15.690
Hmm?

00:22:15.690 --> 00:22:17.900
Mannen?

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:21.560
And you've got to... protect your mom.

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:22.480
All right.

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:24.850
Next, we'll tell you about ourselves.

00:22:24.850 --> 00:22:27.650
Info about us'll cost you.

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:30.600
However, that's all for today.

00:22:30.600 --> 00:22:34.020
Drop in again if you want to hear more.

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:36.150
We'll be waiting.

00:22:36.150 --> 00:22:38.100
Let's go, Mannen!

00:22:39.560 --> 00:22:41.850
I'll knock you off your feet

00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:44.020
with a shot to the heart!

00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:55.350
Hey, if I protect a bunch more people,
will Koito come back to life?

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:56.900
She will, right?!

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:02.020
Next time

00:22:58.060 --> 00:22:59.480
To be continued.
